# REGRESSION — A1 cell of the callable-indirection axis: a `Callable`-typed
# LOCAL bound to an `&`-param function writes through on indirect call.
#
# AXIS / CELL (root x callable-provenance x arg-spelling):
#   plain-local int root  x  LOCAL callable  x  `&`-spelled arg
# Sibling: `sound_callable_amp_param_projection.gg` covers the PARAM-callable +
# projection-root cell of the same axis.
#
# ⚠ READ THE FILENAME CAREFULLY. `_amp_param_` names the CALLEE's `&`-parameter
# signature (`void bumpint(int &n)`), NOT how the callable is bound: the
# callable here is a LOCAL, declared inside `main`.
#
# Pre-Track-B1 (measured on gorget-1 base): `gg check` OK, `gg build` OK, binary
# exit 139 (SIGSEGV); under ASan, `SEGV on unknown address 0x29 ... in bumpint`.
# Fix wires `callable_param_types` + `callable_param_ownerships` sidecars on the
# callable-typed local and routes each indirect-call arg through `lower_call_arg`
# on the callee's sig at both `__callable_N` and `__gorget_closure_call_N` arms.
#
# INTENDED: `bumpint` increments the caller's `x`, so the program prints 42 and
# exits 0. The seed is computed, not a literal, so no const-fold can elide the
# call.
#
# ORACLE (ggdef): OUT OF SUBSET — "unresolved local `bumpint`"; ggdef does not
# reify a named function into a `Callable` value. Recorded explicitly per Core #9.
int seed():
    return 41

void bumpint(int &n):
    n = n + 1

void main():
    int x = seed()
    Callable[void(int &)] f = bumpint
    f(&x)
    print(x)
